1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,560
Maya's bakery just won its biggest

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:03,460
order ever:

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,640
a supermarket wants 12,000 loaves a month.

4
00:00:07,169 --> 00:00:08,997
The supermarket will pay her forty

5
00:00:08,997 --> 00:00:10,301
thousand dollars.

6
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:13,209
Flour and wages cost 30,000.

7
00:00:13,629 --> 00:00:15,409
That leaves 10,000 in profit.

8
00:00:16,019 --> 00:00:17,579
But the flour and the wages

9
00:00:17,579 --> 00:00:18,619
are due now.

10
00:00:19,119 --> 00:00:21,239
The supermarket pays in 60 days.

11
00:00:21,804 --> 00:00:23,784
Maya has only 12,000 in the

12
00:00:23,784 --> 00:00:24,064
bank.

13
00:00:24,604 --> 00:00:26,084
The moment she pays her bills,

14
00:00:26,604 --> 00:00:28,144
she is 18,000 short.

15
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:29,880
So her bank lends her the

16
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:30,320
difference,

17
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,400
and the loan is repaid the

18
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,060
day the supermarket pays.

19
00:00:34,655 --> 00:00:37,295
Profitable businesses rarely fail from losses.

20
00:00:37,915 --> 00:00:39,535
They fail when the cash runs

21
00:00:39,535 --> 00:00:40,175
out first.

